<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module header maps each law to Campas/Abzhanov/Fritz/Soons and to the Lean 4 module `MathOfBiology.Loop_070` (L1-L64); Section 4b opens with a design banner (L584-L605) and every FEM function carries a docstring naming the source (Gibson-Ashby L637, Soons load cases L987, Herrel/Campas bite forces L1075, Soons 2012 ablation L1178); the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-5 with single-range `code_locus` values pointing at the current lines. Deductions: uncited geometry constants — lower-mandible factors (L198), 3D half-width exponent (L213), base dimensions 11.4/7.6/6.8 mm and Gaussian field centres/widths (L397-L405) (-4); the structural-peak exclusion zones, tip plate depth and contact-patch width are coded as defaults without a citation (L666-L719, L785-L861) (-3); `mean_tapered_beam_tip_over_base_ratio` and `section_fem_over_beam_*` (L1120-L1124) are computed but surfaced only in a note (-2); the comparison figure's bite-force axis still cites 'Herrel et al.' without a year/venue (L1740) (-1); `--verify-only` duplicates `--self-test` (L2178) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L198–L213: Lower-mandible factors (-0.34, 0.88, 0.90) and 3D half-width 0.48 x^0.82 are model inventions without a source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L198-L213>",
        "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L397–L405: Bmp4/CaM Gaussian field centres/widths and base dimensions 11.4/7.6/6.8 mm are uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L397-L405>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: exact upper-triangular affine group and analytic inverse (L154-L172), Bmp4/CaM field and RCAS suite (L377-L461), and the new reduced FEM — a correct vectorised Q4 plane-stress formulation (2x2 Gauss, symmetric positive-definite D, exact linearity 2F -> 2 sigma) verified against Euler-Bernoulli and Timoshenko (L744-L782, L785-L861, L935-L971), Gibson-Ashby E_trab = E_s (BV/TV)^2 (L636-L641), a two-material shell/core map (L722-L735), three Soons-type load cases (L974-L1064) and 5 machine-checked Lean theorems. Deductions: the 14-species 'empirical' profiles are the forward transform plus Gaussian noise (L266-L272), so the headline collapse and negative control are circular (-5); the remediation item asked for a micro-CT 3D fracture solver and received a 2D sagittal plane-stress section with uniform out-of-plane thickness W_mm (L763-L782), no crack model, and an artificial 0.7 mm solid-keratin tip clamp (L684) that dominates the tip-biting peaks (-3); the `bmp4_index` used for the r_Bmp4 = 0.9997 correlation is linear in `s_D` by construction (L349-L351) (-1); lower-mandible (-0.34, 0.88, 0.90; L198) and 3D half-width (0.48 x^0.82; L213) factors are uncited model inventions (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L266–L272: 14-species 'empirical' profiles are forward_transform_beak_surface() output plus rng.normal(0, 0.0024 s_D) — the collapse tests the inverse of the same transform <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L266-L272>",
