<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — MorphoEval overall 87.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py` (overall weighted score 87.6/100, down from 93.2 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed as an honest reduced model: Section 4b (L584-L1468) adds a two-material plane-stress Q4 finite-element solver for the sheared sagittal upper beak (Gibson-Ashby trabecular core + keratin rhamphotheca) under tip-biting, base-biting and 30 deg oblique seed loads, verified against Euler-Bernoulli (0.9925) and Timoshenko (0.9905), mesh-converged to 0.45 %, and exercised across all 14 species (tapered-beam slope 0.971, r = 0.9986; CV(sigma)/CV(F) = 0.432; G. magnirostris base-biting bone risk index 0.017). Two new Lean theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys), two new SHA-256-pinned dataset files, two new media outputs, 19 measurements and a 10-check self-test are credited. The score falls because this round exposed defects the v2 audit did not penalise: the 14-species collapse is circular (synthetic profiles from the model's own forward transform, L266-L272); several reference values are the script's own output or Law-2 formula outputs (L1905, L1915, L1955); the species table and the geometry constants (L96-L101, L198, L213, L397-L405) carry no per-value provenance; the Gould specimen D/L is tuned by hard-coded `ref_dl` and a 0.74 perspective factor (L478-L483, L522); the bite-force citation names the wrong venue (L1936); every Pass 3 FEM constant was transcribed offline; and the thin canonical tip is replaced by an artificial 0.7 mm keratin plate (L684) that dominates the 10.8x tip/base stress ratio. Overall 87.6/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py at 8a7928d7, image/png, 573130 B, 2781×1285 px, artifact_sha256 4f214f0596736b346a6af38f147815d628f8ab44dd8430463f6115382d10b90b (sha256 4f214f0596736b346a6af38f147815d628f8ab44dd8430463f6115382d10b90b), spec_fingerprint 69389d287a403dfef90b7be15dfd80b39613de2e2fd62676231e5453b6f3f2f1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 69389d287a403dfef90b7be15dfd80b39613de2e2fd62676231e5453b6f3f2f1; artifact_sha256: 4f214f0596736b346a6af38f147815d628f8ab44dd8430463f6115382d10b90b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_reference.json=cf6430de0c52d725..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/beak_fem_fracture_reference.json=bff86f96d0fcc2fd..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/darwin_finches_specimen.jpg=5ea7ada14a01ba77..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/paper_citations.bib=f0b9fb929ffd2d09..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/pass3_citations.bib=37c2a856e17b123b..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/scout_manifest.json=4b321120fd7b2736...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Campas et al. (2010): upper-beak profiles of the 14 Darwin's finch species collapse onto one master curve under a 3-parameter affine scaling-and-shear group M(s_L, s_D, gamma); Geospiza (Group A) collapse under pure scaling, Camarhynchus/Platyspiza/Cactospiza (Group B) and Certhidea/Pinaroloxias (Group C) need the shear | Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006): Bmp4 scales beak depth/width and calmodulin scales length; RCAS::Bmp4, RCAS::Noggin and RCAS::CaM in chick change beak proportions accordingly | Soons et al. (2010, 2012, 2015): micro-CT finite-element models of Geospiza upper beaks show peak von Mises stress under in vivo bite force far less variable than bite force itself, a stress-reducing role for the keratin rhamphotheca, and lower stresses for base biting than tip biting | Herrel et al. (2005): in vivo bite forces of Darwin's finches scale with head width; reconstructed_in_script: Affine matrix and analytic inverse, canonical culmen curve, 2D/3D conical-parabolic beak surface, 14-species collapse with a pure-scaling negative control, 2D Bmp4/CaM Gaussian mesenchymal field, cantilever bending index W D^3/(12 L), four RCAS conditions, connected-component culmen contour extraction on the Gould (1845) plate, and (Pass 3) a two-material plane-stress Q4 FEM of the sagittal upper-beak section with Gibson-Ashby trabecular core, keratin shell, tip/base/oblique seed loads, beam-theory verification, mesh convergence, 14-species fracture-risk indices, keratin-modulus and BV/TV ablations; transfer_boundary: The 14-species 'empirical' profiles are generated by the script's own forward transform plus Gaussian noise (sigma = 0.24 % of s_D), so the collapse RMS 0.0021 / r = 0.9999 and the 45x negative-control ratio validate the inverse of the same transform, not digitised Campas Fig. 2/3 profiles | The FEM is a 2D sagittal plane-stress idealisation (out-of-plane thickness = W_mm everywhere) of a Law-1 sheared culmen profile with a 0.7 mm solid-keratin tip clamp, not a voxel-resolved micro-CT mesh; all moduli, strengths, thicknesses and the three Soons predictions were transcribed offline from memory and are order-of-magnitude anchors | The 'observed' RCAS D/L values and several reference values equal Law-2 formula outputs or the script's own earlier output, so those comparisons are self-referential; does_not_claim: Reproduction of any digitised Campas, Abzhanov or Soons figure value; a 3D micro-CT finite-element model; crack initiation or propagation; keratin-bone interface failure; mediolateral load asymmetry; per-species provenance of the species table (s_L, s_D, s_W, gamma, bite force)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:1845-1861 (measure_morphoeval) and 2178 — the measurements ignore --seed, --bvtv, --keratin-thickness-mm, --load-angle-deg, --fem-nx/--fem-ny, and --verify-only is a pure alias of --self-test. Forward the CLI parameters (or expose a `measure_morphoeval(params)` signature) and either give --verify-only a distinct meaning or remove it.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:1905, 1915-1917, 1945, 1955 — reference values set to the script's own output (negative control 0.092, Certhidea shear RMS 0.012), to Law-2 formula outputs (RCAS D_over_L_obs), or unsourced (r_DL 0.98). Replace each with a literature value carrying a figure/table locus or mark `reference_source: self-consistency` so measure_outputs.py does not count them as external anchors.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:266-272 (evaluate_14_species_affine_collapse) — the 14-species 'empirical' profiles are forward_transform_beak_surface() plus rng.normal(0, 0.0024 s_D), so RMS 0.0021, r = 0.9999 and the 45x negative-control ratio test the inverse of the model's own transform. Vendor digitised Campas et al. (2010) Fig. 2/3 culmen profiles (or at least the published s_L, s_D, gamma table with figure loci) and collapse those; relabel the current metric as a synthetic self-consistency check.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:478-483 and 522 (segment_darwin_finches_specimen) — hard-coded per-bird ref_dl and the 0.74 'calibrated perspective factor' tune D_over_L_cv toward the references it is correlated with (n = 4). Derive the perspective correction from the plate geometry (or measure it from the image) and source the four reference D/L values to a measured table (e.g. Grant & Grant morphometrics).",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:680-684 (build_beak_fem_mesh) — the x^1.85 canonical culmen gives ~1 % of basal depth at x = 0.1 L, so the tip is clamped to a 0.7 mm solid-keratin plate that dominates the tip-biting peaks (99 MPa for G. magnirostris, 10.8x tip/base ratio vs the 3.07 lever estimate at L2014-2019). Model a real tomial depth and tip thickness (ventral boundary below y = 0) and re-check tip-biting mesh convergence (fem_mesh_convergence at L1215-1227 covers base biting only).",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:763-782 (assemble_plane_stress_stiffness) and 1174-1212 (sweep_keratin_modulus) — uniform out-of-plane thickness W_mm ignores the mediolateral taper of Law 1's 3D surface, mediolateral load asymmetry cannot be represented in 2D, and the keratin ablation substitutes material only, so the geometric (added-thickness) contribution of the rhamphotheca is never separated and the -3.6 % 'shielding' sign conflicts with the recalled Soons (2012) claim. Add a thickness-varying plane-stress (or 3D shell/solid) section and a geometry-with/without-shell ablation.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:96-101, 198, 213, 397-405 — N_POWER, A_0, C_2, ALPHA_*, the lower-mandible factors, the 3D half-width exponent and the Bmp4/CaM Gaussian field centres/widths and base dimensions are uncited. Attach an equation/figure locus to each or label them as free model parameters in the docstring and the math-KG YAML.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/README.md:26-54 — the 'Pass 3 addendum' section appears twice with near-identical content; merge into one section and list the per-value provenance table requested above.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_reference.json `darwin_finch_species` and 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:349-351 — no per-value provenance (paper/figure/table) for s_L, s_D, s_W, gamma_shear, bmp4_index, cam_index, L/D/W_mm or bite_force_N; bmp4_index is linear in s_D so r_Bmp4 = 0.9997 is by construction. Add a `provenance` field per value and replace bmp4_index/cam_index with Abzhanov (2004, 2006) in situ expression scores or drop the correlation.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/beak_fem_fracture_reference.json `provenance_note` and 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py:1936 — every FEM constant and Soons prediction was transcribed offline from memory; the bite-force source is cited as 'Herrel et al. (2005) Evolution' (it is J. Evol. Biol. 18:669-675) and paper_citations.bib has no Herrel entry. Verify all ten DOIs, replace the moduli, strengths and thicknesses with values carrying page/table loci, and fix the venue string." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.76e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 14 species x 3 affine groups (L236-L371), 4 RCAS conditions (L433-L461), and the new FEM parameter axes — BV/TV sweep (L1154-L1171, deflection 12.3 -> 2.0 um, keratin peak 2.39 -> 0.56 MPa), keratin-modulus ablation (L1174-L1212, shielding strictly increasing and exactly 0 at E_k = E_core), load position tip -> base (GIF, L1422-L1468), load angle, keratin thickness and mesh density, all exposed as CLI flags `--bvtv`, `--keratin-thickness-mm`, `--load-angle-deg`, `--fem-nx`, `--fem-ny` and honoured by the FEM figure (L2161-L2199). Deductions: `measure_morphoeval()` ignores every CLI parameter (seed 2010, BV/TV 0.55, 90x18 fixed at L1845-L1861), so the measured values cannot be swept from the command line (-4); `--verify-only` is a pure alias of `--self-test` (L2178) and `--seed` only changes the synthetic noise (-2); the keratin ablation substitutes material only, never separating the added-thickness contribution (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L1845–L1861: measure_morphoeval() hard-codes seed=2010 and FEM defaults; CLI parameters are not forwarded to the measurements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L1845-L1861>",
        "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L2178–L2178: --verify-only is an alias of --self-test <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L2178-L2178>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `--self-test` passes 10/10 checks in ~10.6 s CPU (L2064-L2159) covering both Pass 3 SHA pins, FEM/EB and FEM/Timoshenko within the JSON acceptance, Gibson-Ashby 7000 x 0.5^2 = 1750, D symmetric positive-definite, exact linearity (rtol 1e-9), mesh convergence < 8 %, 14 species, tapered-beam slope and r, keratin-shielding monotonicity with an exact zero at E_k = E_core, BV/TV sweep monotonicity, and 19 measurements each with `reference_value` + `unit`; the default run regenerates all four media files in ~10 s and the growth GIF is byte-identical across runs. Deductions: `docs/media/*.png` is gitignored so the regenerated comparison PNG and the new FEM PNG are not tracked by the repository (-3); the dataset README duplicates its Pass 3 addendum (L26 and L41) (-2); self-test asserts `len(meas) == 19` by count only, not by name, so a renamed measurement would pass silently (L2147-L2149) (-1); no requirements lock file is vendored for this slot (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/README.md L26–L41: Duplicated 'Pass 3 addendum' sections <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/README.md#L26-L41>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Source and data traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: 6 dataset files are SHA-256-pinned and verified at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity` L131-L142; `EXPECTED_PASS3_SHA256` L608-L615 and `load_fem_reference` L621-L633 for the two new files); the new `beak_fem_fracture_reference.json` lists DOIs for Soons 2010/2012/2015, Herrel 2005, Gibson-Ashby 1997 and Seki 2005 with a `used_for` field each, and `pass3_citations.bib` carries the same six entries; the dataset README documents the reduced-model decision. Deductions: the JSON `provenance_note` states that every constant and prediction was transcribed offline from memory and that all DOIs must be re-verified — no DOI was verified in this pass either (-4); the Pass 2 species table (s_L, s_D, s_W, gamma, bmp4_index, cam_index, L/D/W_mm, bite_force_N) has no per-value figure/table provenance (-4); the bite-force source is cited with the wrong venue 'Herrel et al. (2005) Evolution' at L1936 and `paper_citations.bib` has no Herrel entry (-3); `N_POWER`, `A_0`, `C_2`, `ALPHA_*` (L96-L101) are labelled Campas Eq. 1 parameters without a locus (-2); the README carries the Pass 3 addendum twice (L26 and L41) (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L1936–L1936: Bite-force reference cited as 'Herrel et al. (2005) Evolution'; the paper is J. Evol. Biol. 18:669-675 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L1936-L1936>",
        "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L96–L101: N_POWER, A_0, C_2, ALPHA_B/W/C presented as Campas Eq. 1 parameters with no equation/figure locus <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L96-L101>",
        "datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/beak_fem_fracture_reference.json L1–L112: Six sources with DOI and used_for; provenance_note states all constants were transcribed offline from memory <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/beak_fem_fracture_reference.json#L1-L112>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the SHA-256-locked Gould (1845) lithograph is segmented into four culmen contours (L466-L581), the comparison PNG panel E shows the contours, and the new FEM PNG (6 panels) and seed-contact sweep GIF render the von Mises fields on the sheared G. fortis / G. magnirostris sections. Deductions: `spec_defs` hard-codes a per-bird `ref_dl` (L478-L483) and the measured D/L is multiplied by a 0.74 'calibrated perspective factor' (L522), so the r_DL = 0.9588 (n = 4, p = 0.04) is tuned toward the references it is compared with (-5); the FEM geometry is the Law-1 sheared culmen over a flat occlusal plane y = 0 with no real tomial depth or tip thickness, and the ventral boundary is the artificial 0.7 mm plate (L684) (-3); no digitised Campas profile or Soons stress map is vendored for a specimen-level comparison (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L478–L483: Hard-coded per-bird ref_dl values (1.078, 0.965, 0.873, 0.479) that the measured D/L is correlated against <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L478-L483>",
        "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L522–L522: dl_measured scaled by 0.74 'calibrated perspective factor' — a tuning constant without a documented calibration <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L522-L522>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

